#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bale — Claude session orchestrator.

The CLI for the Claude tarball workflow: `bale pack` builds request
tarballs, `bale apply` validates and integrates the response tarballs a
worker Claude returns, `bale open` consumes a planner bundle into a
packed session (verify, dry-run, replay — bin/bale_open.py, board
49a-ii), and the ancillary commands (revert, rollback, retry,
amend-checkpoint, relay, unlock, handoff, config init, status, stats) manage
the session lifecycle around them. BALE.md at the repo root is the canonical design
document — comments below cite its sections. Stdlib-only, Python 3.10+
(3.11+ uses stdlib `tomllib`; 3.10 the vendored parser in
`bin/_bale_toml.py`). The version narrative that once lived here is git
history now — recover any prior revision with a checkout.

Sections:
   1. Imports + constants                                 (~line   300)
   2. Logging                                             (~line   380)
   3. Shell / git helpers                                 (~line   465)
   4. Hashing                                             (~line   515)
   5. Session IDs and the per-day counter                 (~line   535)
   6. Session registry + locks                            (~line   635)
   7. .gitignore handling for the .bale/ directory        (~line  1310)
   8. Path safety + inbound path resolution               (~line  1340)
   9. Editor invocation                                   (~line  1475)
  10. Baleignore matching (pack filter chain + apply rule 14) (~line  1535)
  19. Revert                                              (~line  1785)
  20. Retry                                               (~line  2130)
  28. Amend-checkpoint                                    (~line  2320)
  21. Unlock                                              (~line  2680)
  22. Handoff                                             (~line  2990)
  23. Hook invocation                                     (~line  3670)
  24. Help and completion                                 (~line  3830)
  25. Status                                              (~line  4235)
  27. Stats                                               (~line  5005)
  26. CLI                                                 (~line  5065)

Sections 11-15 (the pack path: scope projection + threshold caps, slug
validation, manifest and tarball construction, wizard, pack) were
extracted to bin/bale_pack.py in v0.3.12; slug validation stayed behind,
folded into section 5, and section 10 was retitled to the baleignore
matcher cluster that remains. Sections 16-18 (the apply path: apply
helpers, the apply pipeline, cmd_apply) followed to bin/bale_apply.py in
v0.3.13; of the old apply-helpers section, current_branch and
working_tree_clean stayed behind beside git() in section 3,
resolve_inbound_path in the retitled section 8, and the handoff.md
heading slicers in section 22 beside their consumer. Section numbers
19-26 keep their old values — the banners are the searchable anchors and
every cross-file "section N" comment stays true — so the 11-18 gap is
deliberate, not drift. Section 27 (Stats, v0.3.24) sits physically
before section 26 so the CLI section stays the file's tail; section 28
(Amend-checkpoint, v0.4.17) sits physically between 20 and 21, beside
the lifecycle verbs it corrects for, with a fresh number rather than a
renumbering. Section 29 (Relay, v0.4.18) sat after it for the same
reason — the exchange-thread verb beside the lifecycle verbs it
suspends between — until it was extracted to bin/bale_relay.py in
v0.4.21, behavior-preserving, on the bale_pack/bale_apply pattern: the
sibling owns the verb, this file keeps the CLI wiring. The listing
above is in physical order, the numbers stay stable.
"""

